(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "ADR-2608196200")
  (:adr/title "The first orphan gets a runner")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-19")
  (:adr/body
"ADR-2608196100 counted twelve verifiers with no runner and no twin, and said
the six that read `orgs/` belong in the detector registry -- **one at a time,
each with a measured interval and timeout rather than a guessed one**, because
bulk registration defeats what the registry's `:why` and `:measured` fields are
for.

This is the first one: `verify-source-path-pins`.

## Why it qualifies

It asks whether the checkout behind a shadow-cljs `:source-path` is the revision
`west.yml` pins. A build that compiles a sibling checkout at some other revision
produces an artifact nobody can reproduce, and nothing records which revision
was compiled.

The already-registered `verify-shadow-source-paths` asks whether a declared
`:source-path` **exists**. This asks whether what is behind it is the **pinned**
revision. A build can pass the first and fail this one.

**It has caught nothing, because nothing ever ran it.** The registry's `:why`
field demands what a detector would have caught, with a date, and the honest
answer is a present measurement rather than a past catch: 2026-08-19, **240 of
383** cross-repo source-paths resolve to a revision `west.yml` does not pin. The
property is violated at scale right now, and NEW/RESOLVED is what turns that
standing number into a signal when it moves.

## Measured, not guessed

16s wall on two consecutive runs, at load 7.6 and 8.3; 383 source-paths across
31 `shadow-cljs.edn`; 240 findings; exit 1. Interval 6h, timeout 10m -- sized
against contention rather than against the quiet number, following
`verify-layer-deps`'s precedent.

Exit 1 is fine and the entry says why: the tick's `:status` is **never `:ok` on
the strength of an exit code alone** -- the evidence regex has to match, and
this detector prints `SCANNED<TAB>383` before any finding.

## Two things the first run taught

**`{{root}}` is passed explicitly**, because the script's default root is a
hardcoded absolute path to this machine's checkout. A tick running from a
worktree would otherwise scan the wrong tree and find nothing.

That is not hypothetical: the first test run *was* from a worktree, and the
result was

    verify-source-path-pins → inconclusive exit 2, 0 finding(s), scanned=0
    no evidence line matching /SCANNED\\t[1-9][0-9]*\\t/
    REFUSING to report a pass: no cross-repo source-path was examined

**The framework refused to call an empty scan clean**, and the detector refused
too, independently. Two floors caught the same mistake, which is what they are
for. Re-run with `--root` at the orgs-bearing checkout, it reports findings
normally.

## Remaining

Five of the six `orgs/`-reading orphans are still unregistered:
app-content-address, d1-kotobase-migration, duplicate-registrations, kip-quorum,
kotoba-pages. `kotoba-pages` cannot be registered as-is -- it launches
Playwright and this machine has no browser installed, so it dies in 0s.
`duplicate-registrations` exits 0 today and spends 55s in 10 `gh` invocations,
which is a different cost profile and deserves its own reading before it gets an
interval.")))
